*Scoping* | V-$CHIPVR ($CHIPCN)

RR2 implements a simple two-level scoping model where variables and functions belong to either file scope or function scope.

*Scope Levels*

''File Scope'' - Variables and functions declared at the top level of a file or within ''if'', ''while'', or ''for'' blocks are accessible throughout the entire file after declaration.

''Function Scope'' - Variables declared inside a function body are local to that function and cannot be accessed from outside.

*Block Behavior*

Chip's ''if'', ''while'', and ''for'' blocks do not create new scopes. Variables declared inside these blocks belong to their parent scope:

'''
var x = 5;

if true
{
    var y = 10;  # belongs to file scope
}

var z = y;  # accessible here
'''

*Function Isolation*

Only functions create new scopes. Variables declared in a function are isolated and inaccessible outside:

'''
func MyFunc()
{
    var local = 20;
}

MyFunc();
var x = local;  # Kaboom
'''

I'll probably change this behaviour at some point when it annoys me or causes problems.
